1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,790
33 MINERS WERE TRAPPED 2,300 FEET UNDERGROUND

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,769
THE MINE HAD COLLAPSED ABOVE THEM

3
00:00:06,969 --> 00:00:08,840
THEIR ONLY WAY OUT WAS BLOCKED

4
00:00:09,090 --> 00:00:12,659
FOR 17 DAYS, NOBODY KNEW IF THEY WERE ALIVE

5
00:00:13,259 --> 00:00:15,466
THIS IS THE SAN JOSÉ MINE INCIDENT

6
00:00:15,766 --> 00:00:18,995
IT BEGAN ON THE AFTERNOON OF AUGUST 5, 2010

7
00:00:19,245 --> 00:00:21,543
DEEP IN THE ATACAMA DESERT, IN CHILE

8
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:23,561
IT WAS A COPPER AND GOLD MINE

9
00:00:23,811 --> 00:00:28,628
ITS ONLY WAY IN AND OUT WAS ONE LONG TUNNEL

10
00:00:28,878 --> 00:00:32,054
ABOUT 2,300 FEET DOWN

11
00:00:32,654 --> 00:00:38,560
THEN A BLOCK OF ROCK AS TALL AS A 45-STORY BUILDING BROKE LOOSE

12
00:00:38,810 --> 00:00:40,836
IT SLID DOWN AND CUT THROUGH THE TUNNEL

13
00:00:41,186 --> 00:00:42,532
THERE WAS A HUGE BLAST

14
00:00:42,932 --> 00:00:44,128
DUST FILLED THE MINE

15
00:00:44,428 --> 00:00:46,209
THE ONLY WAY OUT WAS BLOCKED

16
00:00:46,809 --> 00:00:49,512
SOME OF THE MEN CLIMBED UP A VENTILATION SHAFT

17
00:00:49,762 --> 00:00:53,381
BUT PART OF ITS EMERGENCY LADDER HAD NEVER BEEN INSTALLED

18
00:00:53,631 --> 00:00:55,017
SO THEY COULD NOT GO ON

19
00:00:55,617 --> 00:00:58,306
THEIR SHIFT BOSS, LUIS URZÚA, TOOK CHARGE

20
00:00:58,556 --> 00:01:00,061
THEY GATHERED IN THE SHELTER

21
00:01:00,311 --> 00:01:02,143
A SMALL ROOM DEEP IN THE MINE

22
00:01:02,543 --> 00:01:05,567
ITS EMERGENCY FOOD WAS MEANT TO LAST 2 DAYS

23
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:06,973
THEY MADE IT LAST

24
00:01:07,273 --> 00:01:12,696
EVERY OTHER DAY: A BITE OF TUNA, A SIP OF MILK, HALF A CRACKER

25
00:01:13,296 --> 00:01:16,697
UP ON THE SURFACE, THEIR FAMILIES CAMPED OUTSIDE

26
00:01:16,997 --> 00:01:18,360
THEY CALLED IT CAMP HOPE

27
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:20,553
RESCUERS TRIED TO REACH THE MEN

28
00:01:20,803 --> 00:01:23,600
BUT ON AUGUST 7, THE MOUNTAIN MOVED AGAIN

29
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:26,838
NOW THE ONLY WAY TO REACH THEM WAS TO DRILL

30
00:01:27,138 --> 00:01:28,403
DOWN INTO THE MOUNTAIN

31
00:01:28,703 --> 00:01:29,792
TOWARD THE SHELTER

32
00:01:30,292 --> 00:01:32,019
UNDERGROUND, THE FOOD RAN OUT

33
00:01:32,319 --> 00:01:34,525
THE MEN HAD ONLY SIPS OF DIRTY WATER

34
00:01:34,825 --> 00:01:37,370
AND DAYS WENT BY WITH ALMOST NOTHING TO EAT

35
00:01:37,970 --> 00:01:40,227
ON AUGUST 22, BEFORE DAWN

36
00:01:40,528 --> 00:01:43,247
RIGHT NEXT TO THE SHELTER, A DRILL BROKE THROUGH

37
00:01:43,547 --> 00:01:46,267
2,257 FEET DOWN

38
00:01:46,667 --> 00:01:48,446
THE MEN KNOCKED ON THE DRILL PIPE

39
00:01:48,846 --> 00:01:50,560
THEN THEY TIED A NOTE TO ITS TIP

40
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:53,033
ON THE SURFACE, THE DRILL WAS PULLED UP

41
00:01:53,333 --> 00:01:54,778
AT ITS TIP WAS A NOTE

42
00:01:55,078 --> 00:01:56,076
WRITTEN IN RED

43
00:01:56,476 --> 00:01:59,549
“WE ARE FINE IN THE SHELTER, THE 33.”

44
00:02:00,049 --> 00:02:03,547
THAT AFTERNOON, CHILE'S PRESIDENT HELD IT UP FOR THE CAMERAS

45
00:02:03,947 --> 00:02:05,654
ALL 33 WERE ALIVE

46
00:02:06,154 --> 00:02:08,791
BUT THEY WERE STILL 2,300 FEET DOWN

47
00:02:09,091 --> 00:02:12,016
OFFICIALS WARNED IT COULD TAKE MONTHS TO GET THEM OUT

48
00:02:12,716 --> 00:02:14,077
FOLLOW FOR PART 2

